title: containers->kill still returns undef while the other state changes return 1/0
updated: 2026-08-27T15:55:35Z
---

Fallout from #16, which routed start/stop/restart/pause/unpause through
_state_change so they answer 1 (changed, 204) or 0 (already so, 304).

kill was correctly left out: it never answers 304. It is 204, or 409 when
the container is not running, and 409 croaks. So there is no second outcome
for a flag to carry.

The consequence is a surface that now reads inconsistently - kill is
state-change-shaped, sits next to five methods that report what they did,
and returns undef. Either it joins them (always 1, since reaching the return
means the signal was delivered), or the POD says in one sentence why it does
not. Measured behaviour first: check what the engine actually answers for
kill on a stopped container before deciding.
